comment.narrative:
CEDRO V:
Innovation, Entrepreneurship and Research: 
- 5 start-ups were selected for the accelaration phase in Q3 2022 and accelaration phase completed in Q3 2022;
- Energy audit RFQ for 1 site was completed;
- Energy audit RFQ for 9 sites was launched, evaluated, and contract was awaraded with works ongoing ;

Technology Transfer:
- 2 Solar PV sites completed in Q4 2022;
- 3 Solar PV sites ongoing;
- 1 non-concentrated solar thermal site was completed in Q2 2022;
- Energy Efficiency (EE) Backstopping firm hired for designing, ternder prepararation, and follow up for 3 EE sites in Q3 2022;
- Concentrated solar thermal (CST) consultant was hired for designing, tender preparation, and follow up for CST site in Q4 2022;
- Biogas consultant was hired for designing, tender preparation, and follow up for CST site in Q4 2022;
ARZ Certification: 
- ARZ Building Rating System online in Q4 2022;
- 4 workshops done forARZ Building Rating System online in Q4 2022;
-  Development of Regulatory and Fiscal Instruments for Green Buildings  report in Q4 2022;

ALI: 
- Digitalizing Data Collection Survey for Ministry of Industries in Q4 2022;
- Launching online Energy Efficiency Audits for Industries in Q4 2022;
- Roadmap for energy data collection for industries published in Q4 2022;

REC Establishment:
- Legal assistance provided for regulatory framework provision for RECs in Q2 2022;
- Issuer agreement with LCEC was signed in Q1 2022;
- I-REC trained LCEC on the IREC platform in Q3 and Q4 2022;
- LCEC prepared  Registrant Agreement  and  Fee Structure , and both documents were approved by I-REC in Q3 2022;

Capacity Building:
- TTT Program for Biogas and Energy Efficiency was implemented in Q4 2022
- Internship program for 100 engineering students was done in Solar PV, Solar thermal, and career guidance in Q3 2022;
- Crowfunding Workshop done in 4 regions for 80 municipalities in Lebanon and a Guideline Report was developped on Crowdfunding;

Policy and communication:
- 7 Energy Espresso Podcasts launched online in Q1 2022
- 5 Testimonial Videos
- 14 Educational videos in Q2 2022
- Crowfunding videos 
- 13 fact sheets
- 6 Start-up videos in Q3 2022
- 2publications in Q3 2022

CEDRO V (COVID):
Activity 1.3. Implementing solar for health initiatives
1- Completion of the installation of solar PV systems for the originally selected 10 public hospitals together with the 5 additional hospitals
2- Implementation of solar hot water systems for the selected 10 public hospitals (to maintain/upgrade and install new systems)
3- Implementation of Lighting retrofit for the originally selected 10 public hospitalstogether with the 2 additional hospitals
4- Establishment of the Energy Strategy for the Lebanese Health Care Sector together with recommendations for new buildings designs
5- Implementation of a Computerized Maintenance Management System for 10 public hospitals
6- Implementation of Building Management Systems for 8 hospitals
7- Implementation of Variable Frequency Drives Systems for 9 hospitals

Innovation, Entrepreneurship and Research: 
- RFP for Energy Hub to be launched in Q1 2021; 
- Completion of TORs for the energy audit firm;
- Completion of preliminary design of selected sites.

Implementation of SEACAPS/SEEAP:
- Setting up a crowdfunding platform & uploading selected projects for funding.

ARZ Certification: 
- Develop portal for online ARZ rating
- Implement 4 workshops on train the trainers for ARZ full certification

REC Establishment:
- Legal assistance provided for regulatory framework provision for RECs.

Policy and communication:
- CEDRO 5 website is developed.

 Response to COVID KfW - Solar for Health and Solid Waste intervention:
-Establishment of project team;
- Consultants to design and draft tender documents for solar PV and solar hot water systems are on board;
- Implementation of Solar PV for up to 10 public hospitals is initiated;
- Implementation of solar hot water (to maintain/upgrade and install new systems) for 10 public hospitals is initiated;
- Lighting technologies are upgraded in 10 public sector hospitals; 
- Energy audit for all public hospitals in Lebanon are initiated, and health-care sustainable energy strategy is established.

Project Management
- Initiation of the project;
- Recruitment of staff;
- Procurement of backstopping firm;
Innovation, Entrepreneurship and Research
- Procurement of incubator and energy market need assessment;
- Beneficiary selection and site inspection; 
Implementation of E&E applications:
- TOR for energy audit firm;
- procurement of web application company;
- Assessment of IREC applications in Lebanon;
- Preliminary design of selected sites;
Arz Certification:
- Development of TOR and procurement for ARZ application portal;
Implementation of SEACAPS/SEEAP:
- Selection of 10 pilot projects under SEACAPS;
- Procurement for 5 SEACAP sites;
- Beginning of execution of 5 selected sites;
- setting up a crowdfunding platform & uploading selected projects for funding;
REC Establishment:
- Setting up legal framework for I-REC;
Policy and communication:
- Development of net metering policy initiatives;
- Preparation of website development.

Project Management: 
- Full team is onboard and activities planned and initiated.

Innovation, Entrepreneurship and Research: 
- Procurement of incubator launched in Q3 2020; contract signed in Q4 2020;
- Scale up survey launched in Q2 2020 and results published in Q4 2020;
- Procurement of backstopping firm: following the non-responsiveness to the first bidding launched in Q1 2020, separate RFPs (per technology) will be launched in Q1-2 2021. 

Implementation of RE/EE applications:
- Beneficiary selection and site inspection: beneficiary form launched in Q3 2020; Beneficiary site visit assessment completed in Q4 2020. 

ARZ Certification: 
-Market and ARZ1.0 background assessment submitted in Q2 2020; 
-The online tool procurement and development launching was in Q4 2020. 

Implementation of SEACAPS/SEEAP: 
-11 pilot projects identified under SEACAPS;
-Implementation of Batch 1 (5 sites) started in Q4 2020;
-Bidding document for batch 2 (6 sites) launched in Q4 2020. 

REC Establishment: 
-I-REC delivered report on understanding EAC Schemes and Roadmaps for their development; 
- Setting up legal framework for I-REC; 
- Assessment of IREC applications in Lebanon: Overview of the IREC application worldwide and assessment of its application in Lebanon submitted in Q3 2020. 

Policy and communication:
- Development of net metering policy initiatives;
- Preparation of website development: contract signing in Q4 2020.ts for website upgrade finalized (tendering to launch in Q3 2020)
